# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Every real route is emitted as its own dist/<route>/index.html at build time, and dist/404.html
# makes Pages return a genuine 404 for anything else (it previously served index.html with a 200 —
# a soft 404 that Lighthouse caught via the llms.txt audit).
#
# /auth/* is the one route that cannot be a static file: it is a wildcard that forwards emailed
# verify/reset links to the beta app, so the path is not known ahead of time. This rewrite (200,
# not a redirect) hands those to the SPA shell. It is scoped to /auth/ only, so it cannot shadow
# any prerendered page.
# Permanent redirects, at the edge.
#
# Both were client-side <Navigate replace> only: the server answered 200 with the SPA shell and the
# browser rewrote the URL after React booted. A crawler sees two URLs serving the same page and no
# redirect signal, so link equity is not consolidated. SEO_METADATA_ALL_PAGES.md calls for an
# "Edge-301" on the catalogue spelling specifically.
#
# The React routes stay in place as a fallback for anyone already inside the SPA.
/pricing                          /subscribe                       301
/product/catalogue-intelligence   /product/catalog-intelligence    301

# /auth/* is a wildcard forwarding emailed verify/reset links to the beta app, so it cannot be a
# static file. A 200 rewrite hands it to the SPA shell. Scoped to /auth/ so it cannot shadow a
# prerendered page.
/auth/*  /index.html  200
